    {
      "evidence": "docs/engineering/agent-workflow.md says: \"`--repair-provider` names the provider behind the writer command and is required\". In template/scripts/lifecycle_workers.py `main`, the check is `if \"repair\" in kinds and (args.run or args.providers) and not args.repair_provider`. A plain `work-next --kinds repair` without `--run` or `--providers` (claim only, unfiltered) is accepted. This matches the lifecycle-workers spec and design (\"`--run` for repair requires `--repair-provider`\"), so the code is correct and the guide wording is too broad.",
      "id": "repair-provider-required-wording",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The operating guide says `--repair-provider` is required for repair workers, but the code only requires it with `--run` or `--providers`."
